Saint Clare was a knight's daughter in Assisi, and her family had planned a splendid marriage for her. One night, at about eighteen, she dragged aside the heavy logs and the stone column that barred a door of her father's house and slipped away. She wanted the one thing all their wealth could not give her: to be poor with Christ, who was laid as a baby in a narrow manger. Her family came after her. In time, so did others who loved her and wanted her safe. What did that poverty mean to her, and what would she give to keep it?
